{# "Sold beyond stock" / "Billed beyond stock" (#326) — the lines somebody deliberately sold or
   billed past what the shelf could cover, with the figures they were looking at and what they
   said about it.

   Absent from almost every document, which is the point: the section appearing at all IS the
   finding. On the DOCUMENT rather than on a worklist, for the reason ShortDatedReceipt gives
   about the Exceptions screen — that screen is a MONEY worklist sorted by what each row puts at
   risk, and an oversell has no amount at risk. The goods are sold, at the price on the line; what
   it is worth is measured in units. It belongs where the person asking about it is standing.

   A notice, not an alarm: `alert warn`, the class the receipt screen uses for pallets it accepted
   with a bad date. Nobody did anything wrong; somebody made a call and put their name on it.

   The order's copy and the invoice's were the same section, the same seven columns and the same
   seven cells, under two headings.

   Parameters
   ----------
   lines               required  ALL the document's lines. The panel picks out the ones carrying a
                                 stockOverride itself, into a plain array rather than with
                                 |filter: |filter hands back an iterator, this is both counted and
                                 looped over, and an iterator that has been counted has already
                                 been walked. Both callers had that loop; now neither does.
   heading             required  'Sold beyond stock' on an order, 'Billed beyond stock' on an
                                 invoice. An order promises; an invoice demands payment.
   quantityColumnLabel required  what the third column counts — 'Asked for' on an order, 'Billed'
                                 on an invoice. It is also the cell's data-label, so the two
                                 cannot drift apart.
   noticeTemplate      required  the paragraph inside the alert, as a TEMPLATE PATH rather than as
                                 a string parameter. The two differ by more than wording: the
                                 order's closes on the figures being a snapshot, with an <em> in
                                 it, and the invoice's closes on backorder capacity never being
                                 cover. Prose carrying its own markup is not a parameter, and
                                 eight parameters to rebuild two sentences would be drift with
                                 extra steps. Rendered with {count: <how many lines>}.
   showBackorderCapacity optional  true to append "(after N backorder capacity)" to the Short by
                                 cell when the override recorded any. The order passes true. The
                                 invoice does not, and its notice says why: an invoice line has no
                                 split to fall back on, so capacity never stood behind those units
                                 and printing it would suggest something covered them.
   sectionStyle        optional  the inline style on the wrapping <section>. Defaults to
                                 'margin-top:20px;'.

   The four figures go through |qty because they are quantities and this application has one rule
   for printing one (App\Service\DisplayNumber): 2.5 reads "2.5", 50 reads "50", and neither reads
   "2.5000". They were bare when the columns were INTEGER and a bare decimal(14, 4) would now print
   its trailing zeros. Nothing here posts, so none of these is a `*_rendered` twin and
   LineDenomination::boxUntouched() is not involved — these are <td> cells on a detail screen. #}

{% set overrideLines = [] %}
{% for line in lines %}
    {% if line.stockOverride %}{% set overrideLines = overrideLines|merge([line]) %}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% if overrideLines is not empty %}
    <section class="table-card no-search no-paginate detail-page-card" id="stock-overrides" style="{{ sectionStyle|default('margin-top:20px;') }}">
        <div class="table-header"><h2>{{ heading }}</h2></div>
        <div style="padding:0 20px 8px;">
            <p class="alert warn">
                {% include noticeTemplate with {count: overrideLines|length} only %}
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="wide-table-wrap">
            <table class="user-manager-table" id="stock-override-table" style="min-width:100%;">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Line</th>
                        <th>Region</th>
                        <th style="text-align:center;">{{ quantityColumnLabel }}</th>
                        <th style="text-align:center;">Available then</th>
                        <th style="text-align:center;">Short by</th>
                        <th>Decided by</th>
                        <th>Reason</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    {% for line in overrideLines %}
                        {% set override = line.stockOverride %}
                        <tr id="stock-override-row-{{ override.id }}">
                            <td data-label="Line">{{ line.sku ?: line.name }}</td>
                            <td data-label="Region" id="stock-override-region-{{ override.id }}">{{ override.regionName }}</td>
                            <td data-label="{{ quantityColumnLabel }}" style="text-align:center;" id="stock-override-requested-{{ override.id }}">{{ override.requestedQuantity|qty }}</td>
                            {# Negative is shown as it was measured. A SKU that was already 40 units in the
                               hole when this call was made is a different fact from an empty shelf, and
                               clamping it here would hide which of the two happened. #}
                            <td data-label="Available then" style="text-align:center;" id="stock-override-available-{{ override.id }}">{{ override.availableQuantity|qty }}</td>
                            <td data-label="Short by" style="text-align:center;" id="stock-override-shortfall-{{ override.id }}">
                                {{- override.shortfallQuantity|qty -}}
                                {%- if showBackorderCapacity|default(false) and override.backorderCapacity > 0 %} <small>(after {{ override.backorderCapacity|qty }} backorder capacity)</small>{% endif -%}
                            </td>
                            <td data-label="Decided by" id="stock-override-by-{{ override.id }}">{{ override.overriddenBy ?? 'not recorded' }} &middot; {{ override.overriddenAt|date('Y-m-d H:i') }}</td>
                            <td data-label="Reason" id="stock-override-reason-{{ override.id }}">{{ override.reason }}</td>
                        </tr>
                    {% endfor %}
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </section>
{% endif %}
